  "scope": "B1 board smoke: canonical-vs-legacy comparison for mobilenetv1-v4 (x5 all variants; s100/s600 all variants) and resnet50/152 (s100/s600), mobilenetv2 C++ on s100, negative checks on s100p; two board-found product defects fixed with host regression tests",
  "defects_found_on_board": [
    {
      "id": "B1-D1",
      "found": "x5-4g first run: all 5 entries died with MetadataMismatchError 'The declared raw_f32 contract does not accept output quantization metadata.'",
      "root_cause": "Real X5 mobilenet artifacts ship F32 outputs that still carry a compiler quant descriptor; legacy consumers ignore it. The shared binding rejected descriptor presence instead of gating on dtype.",
      "fix": "dtype is the gate: raw_f32 accepts float32 outputs with a vestigial descriptor (snapshotted in ModelBinding.output_quants, never applied); non-float32 still rejected. Two enforcement sites relaxed in sync: samples/_shared/cls_binding.py bind_model and samples/_shared/quantization.py apply_output_transform; runtime_meta.py/quantization.py docstrings updated.",
      "regression_tests": "generated tests/test_binding.py: test_bind_model_keeps_vestigial_quant_descriptor_on_f32_output + test_bind_model_rejects_quantized_output_dtype_for_raw_f32 (all 4 mobilenet samples); resnet test_binding.py: test_declared_raw_f32_keeps_vestigial_quant_descriptor; _shared test_quantization.py: test_raw_f32_ignores_vestigial_quant_descriptor"
    },
    {
      "id": "B1-D2",
      "found": "x5-4g first run: 'download.sh x5 medium' fetched the SMALL artifact (medium file never downloaded).",
      "root_cause": "mobilenetv4 model/download.py download_target called asset_reference(target) without forwarding variant; generator template never set variant_call for multi-variant samples. v1-v3 are single-variant and unaffected.",
      "fix": "gen_mobilenet.py variant_call ', variant' in multi-variant branch; v4 download.py line 67 asset_reference(target, variant); re-render verified byte-identical for all 4 samples' generated files.",
      "regression_tests": "new generated tests/test_download.py per mobilenet sample: download_target with stubbed downloader must hand the exact published reference per (target[,variant]) to download_asset — 3 targets x v1-v3, 6 combos for v4",
      "board_proof": "x5-4g v4/medium row passed after fix (artifact fb09f1ee14c764db..., distinct from small 4e7f8c57f607d45d...)"
    }
  ],
  "harness_fixes_not_product": [
    "runner canonical side initially omitted labels (ClassificationTask(labels=...)) so labels_equal compared names vs ids — fixed by loading datasets/imagenet/imagenet_classes.names via samples._shared.labels.load_labels",
    "negative mode initially expected stale phrases and hit the file-existence check before the identity gate — fixed by staging the s100 artifact first and matching the real error strings ('Target mismatch: requested s100, detected s100p.' / 'No published sample asset matches target='s100p'')"
  ],
